Lets Index::announced_since in index.rs send the record the pending set kept
for a path whatever its seq, as before c659b15. Catch-up can then carry a
record this machine adopted after its last batch and never announced, with a
seq_high that moves the peer's watermark past the withheld pending records,
which that peer then never asks for (DESIGN.md §7.4).

test: delocal-sim regressions::catch_up_never_sends_what_this_machine_has_not_announced
test: delocal-engine index::tests::announced_since_never_sends_a_record_this_machine_has_not_announced

diff --git a/crates/engine/src/index.rs b/crates/engine/src/index.rs
index 4029a94..d26c77a 100644
--- a/crates/engine/src/index.rs
+++ b/crates/engine/src/index.rs
@@ -345,7 +345,7 @@ impl Index {
             .records
             .iter()
             .filter_map(|(path, record)| match self.pending.get(path) {
-                Some(kept) => kept.announced_record.as_ref().filter(announced),
+                Some(kept) => kept.announced_record.as_ref(),
                 None => Some(record).filter(announced),
             })
             .filter(|r| r.seq > after)
